WEBVTT

00:01:30.980 --> 00:01:34.510
"Loss"

00:01:37.350 --> 00:01:39.490
You're reassigning me as an instructor?

00:01:39.940 --> 00:01:40.870
That's right.

00:01:41.390 --> 00:01:42.780
You have two weeks to prepare.

00:01:42.780 --> 00:01:43.890
You will undergo special training

00:01:43.890 --> 00:01:46.320
before taking your post in
Gurantseere Cosmopolitan Academy.

00:01:47.820 --> 00:01:50.200
You were an exceptional pilot.

00:01:50.200 --> 00:01:52.810
This is the optimum post
for making the most of those skills.

00:01:56.080 --> 00:02:03.100
The MJP Project was founded in GC 35
to develop humans suited for space life.

00:02:03.540 --> 00:02:05.310
With the Wulgaru invasion,

00:02:05.310 --> 00:02:08.630
it was decided that those over
the age of 12 were to become pilots.

00:02:08.630 --> 00:02:12.110
They were transferred to
Gurantseere Cosmopolitan Academy.

00:02:12.110 --> 00:02:14.110
Open
SPIRITS

00:02:14.760 --> 00:02:15.860
Congratulations!

00:02:16.470 --> 00:02:18.680
This isn't the sort of
thing you celebrate.

00:02:20.080 --> 00:02:22.870
How could you say that?
Aren't you embarking on a new journey?

00:02:22.870 --> 00:02:25.970
My job is to train children
who were genetically

00:02:25.970 --> 00:02:28.720
altered before birth to fight on the frontline!

00:02:29.480 --> 00:02:30.860
It's depressing...

00:02:32.210 --> 00:02:36.700
Those children were temporarily left
in the care of foster parents,

00:02:36.700 --> 00:02:38.880
but we're going to erase
all of their personal

00:02:38.880 --> 00:02:40.430
memories before they start school.

00:02:41.170 --> 00:02:44.460
I wonder if that's so they won't regret
leaving their old lives behind.

00:02:44.380 --> 00:02:47.420
Dealing with kids that lack both
a past and future...

00:02:47.420 --> 00:02:48.470
I don't know if I can take it.

00:02:48.470 --> 00:02:50.840
Excuse me! Gimme another
medium-sized beer!

00:02:50.840 --> 00:02:52.480
Are you even listening?

00:02:52.480 --> 00:02:54.970
Actually, screw that.
Gimme a bottle of premium saké!

00:02:57.460 --> 00:02:59.950
But isn't that why they
chose you, Rin-Rin?

00:03:02.390 --> 00:03:05.320
True, my piloting and
fighting days are over...

00:03:05.700 --> 00:03:07.360
This is the only job left for me.

00:03:08.060 --> 00:03:10.610
But didn't you make it back alive?

00:03:10.610 --> 00:03:12.940
You were the only survivor
when your unit got destroyed.

00:03:13.730 --> 00:03:15.500
Why don't you pass on
those survival skills?

00:03:19.030 --> 00:03:19.930
Okay?

00:03:40.100 --> 00:03:41.520
Did you get that?

00:03:41.520 --> 00:03:43.150
Thanks to the Ioness Theory,

00:03:43.150 --> 00:03:46.030
there was a substantial
boost in engine efficiency.

00:03:46.030 --> 00:03:49.620
However, the human reaction time
for those piloting the-

00:03:53.320 --> 00:03:55.200
What are you doing in
the middle of class?

00:03:55.200 --> 00:03:56.630
Uh, well, you see...!

00:03:57.040 --> 00:03:57.910
Well?

00:03:57.910 --> 00:03:59.630
Ah, umm, well...

00:04:00.200 --> 00:04:03.550
S-sorry, I didn't mean it like that.

00:04:03.550 --> 00:04:04.740
Sorry, my bad!

00:04:05.820 --> 00:04:06.550
Poopy.

00:04:08.460 --> 00:04:10.340
Oh, my God!

00:04:10.340 --> 00:04:12.550
Your bodyline is like that
of a beautiful Steyr.

00:04:12.550 --> 00:04:16.300
You've shot my heart with your
hot loaded armor-piercing bullets,

00:04:16.300 --> 00:04:17.790
knocking me down!

00:04:20.140 --> 00:04:21.400
How are the students?

00:04:22.140 --> 00:04:25.350
Right. On average,
they are brimming with potential.

00:04:25.350 --> 00:04:27.160
They follow their orders

00:04:27.160 --> 00:04:30.480
and have fast response times
in mock space battles.

00:04:32.780 --> 00:04:36.610
However, there is one team
that is highly problematic.

00:04:37.450 --> 00:04:38.570
How so?

00:04:38.570 --> 00:04:39.870
Sir...

00:04:39.990 --> 00:04:42.960
The team is composed
of students who were

00:04:42.960 --> 00:04:44.890
originally unsuited for teamwork.

00:04:44.890 --> 00:04:48.050
With impressive latent abilities,
they definitely possess hidden potential.

00:04:48.460 --> 00:04:49.880
But they are lacking
on the mental front.

00:04:49.880 --> 00:04:52.170
They are ill oriented for group work.

00:04:52.670 --> 00:04:53.560
I see.

00:04:54.230 --> 00:04:56.600
That will be their downfall as pilots.

00:04:57.180 --> 00:04:58.430
And the flip side?

00:04:59.890 --> 00:05:02.640
Inversely, they could
become mentally strong.

00:05:02.640 --> 00:05:07.190
Once they master teamwork,
they will outstrip the other teams.

00:05:07.190 --> 00:05:08.690
Uh, on what grounds...?

00:05:08.690 --> 00:05:11.330
They have abnormally strong
survival instincts.

00:05:11.950 --> 00:05:13.440
That makes them ideal pilots

00:05:13.440 --> 00:05:15.670
for AHSMB units equipped
with the JURIA-SYSTEM.

00:05:17.280 --> 00:05:19.590
Train them! That is your mission.

00:05:23.080 --> 00:05:24.200
Very well.

00:05:28.170 --> 00:05:29.540
Tamaki!

00:05:32.010 --> 00:05:34.520
Rose 3's first and second thrusters
have taken damage.

00:05:35.050 --> 00:05:36.760
Power is down by 40%!

00:05:36.760 --> 00:05:39.690
Enemy fighters are
approaching from β34.

00:05:41.390 --> 00:05:43.380
Th-they got me!

00:05:43.380 --> 00:05:45.270
What should we do?! What should I do?!

00:05:45.270 --> 00:05:47.200
Kei, can't we help her?!

00:05:47.810 --> 00:05:49.530
Kei? Kei!

00:05:56.280 --> 00:05:58.280
Calm down. Think.

00:05:58.280 --> 00:05:59.490
I should be able to save her.

00:05:59.490 --> 00:06:02.040
If I'm a hero, fight! Fight!

00:06:02.340 --> 00:06:03.830
Fight so we can survive!

00:06:04.080 --> 00:06:05.580
Harmonic values, increasing.

00:06:05.580 --> 00:06:07.040
One through three are increasing!

00:06:07.620 --> 00:06:08.800
My armguards?

00:06:09.580 --> 00:06:13.480
If Red 5 removed its armguards,
I could use them as shields...?

00:06:22.580 --> 00:06:24.220
Thank you, Red 5!

00:06:24.930 --> 00:06:27.470
Let's go! You're going
to become a hero with me.

00:06:28.180 --> 00:06:30.030
Send a multi-launcher, please!

00:06:43.200 --> 00:06:44.650
Izuru!

00:06:44.650 --> 00:06:46.260
Are you all right, Tamaki?

00:06:46.450 --> 00:06:49.260
Forget about me! Everyone,
get out of here.

00:06:49.260 --> 00:06:50.970
Get a grip, Tamaki!

00:06:51.230 --> 00:06:53.550
But at this rate, they'll take you and
everyone else down with me!

00:06:54.000 --> 00:06:55.470
We're going to make it back alive!

00:06:57.050 --> 00:06:58.770
I... I...!

00:06:59.760 --> 00:07:01.940
I've always wanted to go on a date!

00:07:02.210 --> 00:07:04.440
Even if we make it back,
that may not happen...

00:07:04.440 --> 00:07:06.440
What's with that serious answer?!

00:07:06.890 --> 00:07:08.440
That's not what you say
at a time like this!

00:07:08.680 --> 00:07:10.370
Just tell her she'll find a date!

00:07:10.370 --> 00:07:11.560
Scum.

00:07:13.060 --> 00:07:15.230
Blue 1, take the right.

00:07:15.230 --> 00:07:18.030
Gold 4, take the left.
Purple 2, issue orders.

00:07:18.030 --> 00:07:18.700
Roger!

00:07:19.500 --> 00:07:22.740
Blue 1, strike Unit 4 in the upper right
portion of Formation A.

00:07:22.740 --> 00:07:25.620
Gold 4, fire at the bottom left
portion of Formation B.

00:07:25.620 --> 00:07:28.710
Keep them in check and
carve open a path for Rose 3.

00:07:36.110 --> 00:07:40.260
Ally units have taken 32.6% damage.
Ammo down to 10%.

00:07:40.260 --> 00:07:42.140
They can only fight for
another 12 minutes.

00:07:42.780 --> 00:07:44.840
Probability of return: -15%.

00:07:44.840 --> 00:07:47.050
They can't possibly continue to fight!

00:07:47.050 --> 00:07:50.150
Vice Chief of Staff, please issue
the order for them to retreat.

00:07:51.520 --> 00:07:52.400
Sir!

00:07:53.310 --> 00:07:55.980
Retreat is not an option!
Don't run! Fight the beasts!

00:07:55.980 --> 00:07:58.860
They can't! At this rate,
we're going to lose all of the units.

00:07:58.860 --> 00:08:00.150
Why can't they?!

00:08:00.150 --> 00:08:03.040
Do you realize how much money
we've put into them?

00:08:15.160 --> 00:08:17.850
Blue 1, Gold 4, Red 5, attack!

00:08:18.090 --> 00:08:19.040
Uh, right!

00:08:19.040 --> 00:08:21.140
D-don't turn and run!

00:08:21.510 --> 00:08:23.480
I'm having control issues here!

00:08:24.310 --> 00:08:27.190
Vice Chief of Staff, please
order them to retreat!

00:08:28.840 --> 00:08:30.200
All units, retreat!

00:08:30.680 --> 00:08:32.770
Force Rose 3 to purge.

00:08:32.770 --> 00:08:33.320
Roger.

00:08:33.960 --> 00:08:37.230
Purple 2, forcibly purge
Rose 3. Copy that?

00:08:37.230 --> 00:08:37.830
Yes, Ma'am!

00:08:40.830 --> 00:08:41.950
I'm light!

00:08:41.950 --> 00:08:43.240
Rose 3, retreat!

00:08:43.240 --> 00:08:43.830
Roger!

00:08:47.820 --> 00:08:50.420
If we use Rose 3's
boosters as missiles...

00:08:50.420 --> 00:08:52.460
They should pack a real wallop!

00:09:00.500 --> 00:09:02.960
Blue 1, protect Rose 3 as you retreat.

00:09:02.960 --> 00:09:04.810
Gold 4, serve as backup
while you retreat.

00:09:05.010 --> 00:09:06.810
Red 5, slow withdrawal.

00:09:07.200 --> 00:09:07.930
How's everyone doing?

00:09:07.930 --> 00:09:09.270
They'll reach the ship in just a minute.

00:09:10.470 --> 00:09:11.760
Kei, you should head back as well!

00:09:11.760 --> 00:09:12.530
Roger!

00:09:26.900 --> 00:09:27.620
Izuru!

00:09:28.410 --> 00:09:30.090
Izuru, are you all right?

00:09:31.330 --> 00:09:32.090
Probably.

00:09:32.700 --> 00:09:35.040
Red 5's transmission has been damaged.

00:09:35.040 --> 00:09:38.090
Primary reactor has ceased functioning.
Energy reserves down by 25%.

00:09:38.620 --> 00:09:40.290
Auxiliary power is dropping fast!

00:09:40.290 --> 00:09:42.040
Auxiliary thrusters are totally shot.

00:09:42.040 --> 00:09:43.370
He can't change its course.

00:09:43.840 --> 00:09:45.540
The emergency escape unit is out, too!

00:09:46.530 --> 00:09:48.350
We'll have to cut our
losses with the one.

00:09:48.350 --> 00:09:49.100
Wha-?!

00:09:51.010 --> 00:09:52.900
You aren't the least bit okay!

00:09:52.900 --> 00:09:54.860
I'll be fine, so get back, Kei!

00:09:55.180 --> 00:09:56.060
Izuru?!

00:09:56.060 --> 00:09:57.020
Get back!

00:09:59.060 --> 00:10:00.870
Purple 2, come back immediately!

00:10:01.150 --> 00:10:02.120
But Izuru-!

00:10:02.600 --> 00:10:04.580
I'll head on back after you leave.

00:10:05.090 --> 00:10:07.370
How could you say that?!
You can't even move!

00:10:07.740 --> 00:10:09.380
Purple 2, did you hear me?!

00:10:09.860 --> 00:10:11.660
The hero always makes
it back in one piece.

00:10:11.660 --> 00:10:13.370
I can't die in a place like this!

00:10:13.370 --> 00:10:17.130
I still want to draw manga and
eat more of your insanely sweet cakes!

00:10:17.830 --> 00:10:18.380
Izuru...

00:10:23.000 --> 00:10:23.680
Izuru!

00:10:24.130 --> 00:10:25.320
Purple 2!

00:10:37.250 --> 00:10:39.110
AHSMB units...? Allies?!

00:10:39.520 --> 00:10:41.690
That is...Team Doberman!

00:10:41.690 --> 00:10:43.190
Who gave them orders to sortie?

00:10:44.480 --> 00:10:45.400
Commander!

00:10:45.400 --> 00:10:48.870
Team Doberman will hereby retrieve
Red 5 and withdraw.

00:10:52.360 --> 00:10:53.820
Thank you, Sir!

00:10:54.700 --> 00:10:56.540
If there was another able team,

00:10:56.540 --> 00:10:58.810
we should have included them
in the battle to begin with!

00:10:59.200 --> 00:11:00.430
How dare he hold out on me!

00:11:06.170 --> 00:11:07.090
Izuru!

00:11:07.090 --> 00:11:08.600
Purple 2 has returned.

00:11:15.720 --> 00:11:16.560
Is he okay?!

00:11:16.560 --> 00:11:17.890
Should I get a stretcher?

00:11:17.890 --> 00:11:18.610
Better, just in case!

00:11:21.770 --> 00:11:22.610
Izuru?!

00:11:24.310 --> 00:11:25.620
Are you all right, Izuru?

00:11:26.520 --> 00:11:28.620
The Wulgaru army has
started to pull back.

00:11:29.070 --> 00:11:31.170
I believe they are
headed toward Jupiter.

00:11:42.870 --> 00:11:44.000
Izuru!

00:11:44.000 --> 00:11:45.140
Welcome back!

00:11:45.140 --> 00:11:46.420
Care for a drink?

00:11:48.450 --> 00:11:49.400
Izuru?

00:11:50.430 --> 00:11:51.500
I made it back...

00:11:54.130 --> 00:11:55.240
You should have...

00:11:56.340 --> 00:11:59.060
You should have gotten out of there
with the rest of us.

00:11:59.060 --> 00:11:59.890
What?!

00:11:59.890 --> 00:12:01.650
You don't need to handle
everything by yourself.

00:12:02.050 --> 00:12:04.690
Do you realize what would have
happened if help hadn't come?

00:12:04.690 --> 00:12:06.060
Seriously!

00:12:06.060 --> 00:12:08.910
Ah, everyone is giving
me a piece of their mind.

00:12:09.400 --> 00:12:10.400
Excuse me?!

00:12:10.400 --> 00:12:12.170
That's nothing to be happy about!

00:12:20.290 --> 00:12:23.370
Remove everything from
Block 3 to Block 5.

00:12:23.370 --> 00:12:25.480
Send Rose 3 and Red 5 to Maintenance D.

00:12:25.930 --> 00:12:26.960
Well?

00:12:26.960 --> 00:12:29.430
Ugh. We're administering
emergency repairs,

00:12:29.430 --> 00:12:31.430
but they need a full overhaul in HQ's dock.

00:12:31.430 --> 00:12:33.290
That goes double for Rose 3 and Red 5.

00:12:33.760 --> 00:12:36.100
Rose 3 currently uses
a navigational shield.

00:12:36.100 --> 00:12:38.220
We'll need to give it
a maximum-power shield

00:12:38.220 --> 00:12:39.440
that can withstand enemy beams,

00:12:39.440 --> 00:12:41.880
just like the ones Blue 1 and Red 5 use.

00:12:43.560 --> 00:12:46.490
Really! This is no time for sweets.

00:12:48.730 --> 00:12:50.610
It's time for super-premium dry saké!

00:12:50.610 --> 00:12:51.660
I figured.

00:12:54.870 --> 00:12:56.050
Where is the Vice Chief of Staff?

00:12:56.920 --> 00:12:59.370
Resting in his personal room.

00:12:59.370 --> 00:13:00.360
I see.

00:13:01.330 --> 00:13:04.490
Sir, GDF high command has requested

00:13:04.490 --> 00:13:07.720
we send them a copy of our
battle report in all due haste.

00:13:07.920 --> 00:13:10.470
You write it! I'll check
over it once it's ready.

00:13:12.540 --> 00:13:14.780
I'll send over the battle logs.

00:13:15.580 --> 00:13:16.480
Thank you!

00:13:21.810 --> 00:13:25.020
I wonder how long this war
is going to drag out...

00:13:25.020 --> 00:13:26.020
Who can say?

00:13:26.020 --> 00:13:27.300
We don't even know what

00:13:27.300 --> 00:13:29.920
the Wulgaru are after
or where they came from.

00:13:30.310 --> 00:13:31.730
True enough.

00:13:31.730 --> 00:13:33.820
I'm sorry to have
interrupted your work.

00:13:33.820 --> 00:13:36.240
It's okay. Don't worry about it.

00:13:41.830 --> 00:13:44.410
February 4, 86 GC.

00:13:44.840 --> 00:13:48.580
Our units engaged what
we believe to be an

00:13:48.580 --> 00:13:51.830
armed Wulgaru recon force near FRB-1011.

00:13:55.210 --> 00:14:00.400
That's right. We've been left in
the dark, ever since then...

00:14:01.930 --> 00:14:05.580
They came out of nowhere, striking
Earth's frontier development base.

00:14:06.680 --> 00:14:09.480
The armies stationed around the outer planets
were dispatched immediately.

00:14:09.480 --> 00:14:12.980
Thus began Earth's first
war in outer space.

00:14:14.570 --> 00:14:18.120
We believe the Wulgaru armada is
composed of 1 massive mother ship,

00:14:18.120 --> 00:14:22.330
5 large carriers, 800 space-faring vessels
and 3,000 mobile fighters.

00:14:22.810 --> 00:14:25.790
Our combined global forces
include 15 million soldiers,

00:14:25.790 --> 00:14:28.660
3,500 space-faring vessels and
20,000 mobile fighters.

00:14:29.250 --> 00:14:31.880
Despite vastly superior numbers,

00:14:31.880 --> 00:14:37.090
our results in battle have been dismal
as we gradually pull back.

00:14:38.420 --> 00:14:41.920
At this rate, even the most
favorable calculations

00:14:41.920 --> 00:14:43.470
show them reaching Earth in...

00:14:44.220 --> 00:14:45.780
Isn't this stuff awesome?

00:14:46.270 --> 00:14:48.730
It has a rich fragrance
and a refreshing zing.

00:14:48.730 --> 00:14:52.770
Not to mention the delicious fruity taste
that explodes in your mouth!

00:14:52.770 --> 00:14:54.290
Hey, stop right there!

00:14:54.290 --> 00:14:55.790
S-sorry...

00:14:56.100 --> 00:14:59.210
I swear, you're putting perfectly
good saké to waste!

00:14:59.900 --> 00:15:01.280
Y'know...

00:15:02.410 --> 00:15:05.800
So like, what do you think's
gonna happen to us?

00:15:08.040 --> 00:15:10.170
In this battle, I mean...

00:15:10.790 --> 00:15:11.820
Rin-Rin!

00:15:12.210 --> 00:15:16.270
No matter how much we outnumber them,

00:15:16.270 --> 00:15:18.810
their technology is far superior to our own...

00:15:19.630 --> 00:15:21.880
That may be the case, but...

00:15:25.470 --> 00:15:28.770
Even if we sent a bunch
of men after them,

00:15:28.770 --> 00:15:32.230
they can easily counter the attack
with a handful of cutting-edge units.

00:15:32.230 --> 00:15:33.230
Oh, my, my...

00:15:33.230 --> 00:15:36.000
They swoop in and then
swoop right back out,

00:15:36.000 --> 00:15:39.190
so they've suffered
surprisingly few losses.

00:15:39.510 --> 00:15:41.830
Too many peanuts overwhelm
the persimmon seeds!

00:15:41.830 --> 00:15:43.660
This isn't about persimmon seeds!

00:15:43.660 --> 00:15:45.740
Then what are you talking about?

00:15:47.030 --> 00:15:49.430
Hey! Don't take that attitude with me!

00:15:50.010 --> 00:15:53.000
See, I almost gave up...

00:15:53.420 --> 00:15:55.460
I almost gave up on Red 5.

00:15:55.460 --> 00:15:56.770
Rin-Rin!

00:15:57.630 --> 00:16:01.720
I'm not... supposed to give up
on my own students!

00:16:01.720 --> 00:16:03.990
I'm not supposed to lose hope!

00:16:04.430 --> 00:16:06.390
Aw, jeez...

00:16:07.620 --> 00:16:10.830
Damn, you're a crying drunk...

00:16:17.690 --> 00:16:20.370
Tamaki, go to your room
if you're gonna sleep.

00:16:20.370 --> 00:16:22.870
No! I'm staying here.

00:16:24.030 --> 00:16:25.250
More antacids?

00:16:25.720 --> 00:16:28.950
Isn't it only natural to get an upset stomach
after a battle like that?

00:16:29.240 --> 00:16:31.000
I'm amazed you guys don't have ulcers.

00:16:31.700 --> 00:16:34.890
It's just a matter of time before
you form a hole in your gut.

00:16:35.490 --> 00:16:36.420
Shut it!

00:16:36.420 --> 00:16:39.560
It'd be nice if there was something
we could do to help relax...

00:16:40.460 --> 00:16:43.890
She's crashing in three, two, one!

00:16:45.160 --> 00:16:46.210
Hey!

00:16:48.970 --> 00:16:50.310
Huggie!

00:16:50.310 --> 00:16:51.610
T-Tamaki?!

00:16:52.200 --> 00:16:53.950
She's just like a baby.

00:16:55.120 --> 00:16:57.780
Sometimes, I have dreams.

00:16:58.110 --> 00:16:58.890
Of what?

00:16:59.520 --> 00:17:02.620
I dream that I'm a baby and
someone is holding me.

00:17:05.030 --> 00:17:10.330
When I close my eyes,
someone gently pats me on the back.

00:17:11.110 --> 00:17:12.290
But that's just a dream, right?

00:17:12.630 --> 00:17:16.290
Yeah, but I'm sure someone cared
for me like that once.

00:17:16.290 --> 00:17:17.390
I just don't remember it.

00:17:20.880 --> 00:17:23.600
Say, didn't you think we were
going to die back there?

00:17:25.510 --> 00:17:26.530
Yeah...

00:17:27.660 --> 00:17:31.110
When I die, do you think
they'll inform the people

00:17:31.110 --> 00:17:32.230
who used to pat my back?

00:17:39.520 --> 00:17:40.690
It's doubtful.

00:17:41.480 --> 00:17:43.760
Dang, you're cold!

00:17:44.400 --> 00:17:45.650
Gosh darn it!

00:17:45.650 --> 00:17:48.700
Naïve dudes like you are insensitive
to another's naïve beliefs!

00:17:48.700 --> 00:17:49.530
What was that?!

00:17:49.530 --> 00:17:50.570
Knock it off!

00:17:51.740 --> 00:17:53.870
Yeah. Let's head back to our own rooms.

00:17:54.410 --> 00:17:56.960
Do something about Tamaki before you go.

00:17:56.960 --> 00:17:59.330
Hey, Leader. Carry the girl.

00:18:01.060 --> 00:18:02.230
He's drawing again?

00:18:02.740 --> 00:18:05.000
That's like a tranquilizer for Izuru.

00:18:06.590 --> 00:18:10.740
But Izuru tried to protect
Tamaki, all on his own.

00:18:31.950 --> 00:18:33.020
How do you feel?

00:18:34.160 --> 00:18:35.270
I am fine.

00:18:37.550 --> 00:18:38.460
What is that?

00:18:38.970 --> 00:18:41.220
Supposedly it is called
a "picture book".

00:18:41.750 --> 00:18:45.140
Pictures are drawn to match the story.

00:18:46.550 --> 00:18:49.010
I cannot comprehend such books.

00:18:49.010 --> 00:18:51.190
How could anything save the truth
hold any value?

00:18:51.920 --> 00:18:54.240
I do not understand, myself.

00:18:55.060 --> 00:18:56.690
But they may be unable

00:18:56.690 --> 00:19:00.170
to understand us just as
we fail to understand them.

00:19:03.730 --> 00:19:09.990
Auron Taul has spoken! Open the gate!

00:19:13.530 --> 00:19:18.000
Is fighting the only option for those
who cannot understand one another?

00:19:34.800 --> 00:19:38.530
Team Rabbits will hereby return to
Gurantseere Cosmopolitan Academy.

00:19:38.890 --> 00:19:40.100
Roger!

00:19:40.100 --> 00:19:44.020
We're taking the AHSMB units back to HQ,
where we'll fix them right up.

00:19:44.020 --> 00:19:45.870
Please take me with you, too!

00:19:48.400 --> 00:19:49.830
And one more thing.

00:19:50.650 --> 00:19:52.290
Look after Rin-Rin for me.

00:19:54.570 --> 00:19:57.240
I-I'm just fine!

00:19:57.240 --> 00:20:00.040
You just had a wee bit too much to drink.
Right, Rin-Rin?

00:20:00.040 --> 00:20:02.130
Don't say that in front of my students!

00:20:02.130 --> 00:20:04.160
I wanna call you Rin-Rin!

00:20:04.160 --> 00:20:04.960
Watch it!

00:20:04.960 --> 00:20:06.140
Why do you call her Rin-Rin?

00:20:06.550 --> 00:20:07.880
We're childhood friends.

00:20:07.880 --> 00:20:08.420
Reika!
We're childhood friends.

00:20:08.420 --> 00:20:10.390
I've been calling her that since
elementary school.

00:20:10.830 --> 00:20:13.130
We went to different schools after that,

00:20:13.130 --> 00:20:15.340
but then we met up again at
the military academy, remember?

00:20:17.180 --> 00:20:18.630
Childhood friends...

00:20:20.470 --> 00:20:22.310
I like that backstory!

00:20:22.310 --> 00:20:23.820
This isn't a manga!

00:20:24.310 --> 00:20:27.290
I wonder what it must be like
to have a childhood friend.

00:20:27.290 --> 00:20:29.490
Quit going on about that!

00:20:29.490 --> 00:20:30.730
We'll reach the ground momentarily.

00:20:36.620 --> 00:20:37.620
Rin-Rin, see ya later!

00:20:37.620 --> 00:20:39.670
Like I said, quit calling me that!
Rin-Rin, see ya later!

00:20:40.120 --> 00:20:41.550
Where is the head mechanic going?

00:20:42.120 --> 00:20:44.160
Wasn't she going to GDF's headquarters?

00:20:44.160 --> 00:20:46.670
She said she's dropping
by her home in Kyoto.

00:20:47.740 --> 00:20:49.670
Her family is always
giving her a hard time.

00:20:49.670 --> 00:20:51.680
Believe it or not, she's a rich heiress.

00:20:52.760 --> 00:20:54.010
An heiress?!

00:20:54.010 --> 00:20:55.930
For Saionji Pharmaceutical.

00:20:57.640 --> 00:20:59.210
My sponsor...?

00:20:59.860 --> 00:21:01.720
But she became our head mechanic...?

00:21:01.720 --> 00:21:03.600
Against her parents' wishes.

00:21:03.600 --> 00:21:06.100
They disapproved? How dramatic!

00:21:06.100 --> 00:21:08.230
Your lives are just beginning, too.

00:21:08.230 --> 00:21:12.140
You have a lot to look forward to,
not just fighting.

00:21:13.190 --> 00:21:15.920
Survive this war! That's a must!

00:21:22.570 --> 00:21:23.380
Let's go.

00:21:23.690 --> 00:21:24.660
Okay!

00:21:27.670 --> 00:21:30.590
But dang does my head hurt!

00:21:32.710 --> 00:21:33.850
She's drunk...

00:21:40.470 --> 00:21:42.220
I haven't introduced them yet, have I?

00:21:42.750 --> 00:21:43.860
That is Team Doberman.

00:21:44.730 --> 00:21:47.960
They are the team that rescued you
in that last battle.

00:21:49.190 --> 00:21:51.020
They're your seniors.

00:21:51.020 --> 00:21:53.690
They are second gen MJP students
entering their third term.

00:21:53.690 --> 00:21:56.620
Commander Simon kept them a secret
while they were on standby.

00:21:57.110 --> 00:22:00.480
The team is composed of
Chandra, Randy and Patrick.

00:23:41.010 --> 00:23:56.020
"Operation: Infiltrate a Planetoid Base"
